class ParkingLot {
    private final List<ParkingFloor> floors = new ArrayList<>();

    void addFloor(ParkingFloor f) {            // controlled mutation -> can validate
        Objects.requireNonNull(f);
        floors.add(f);
    }
    List<ParkingFloor> getFloors() {           // read-only view
        return Collections.unmodifiableList(floors);
    }
}
// lot.getFloors().clear();  -> throws UnsupportedOperationException
```
*Mutation goes through `addFloor` (validatable); reads get a view that can't corrupt the source.*

```java
// Every vehicle repeats the same plate/start logic -> duplication
interface Vehicle { String plate(); void start(); }
class Car   implements Vehicle { public void start() { /* same boilerplate */ } }
class Truck implements Vehicle { public void start() { /* copy-pasted again */ } }
```

```java
abstract class Vehicle {                 // shared state + code (IS-A)
    protected final String plate;
    Vehicle(String plate) { this.plate = plate; }
    void start() { System.out.println(plate + " starting"); } // shared once
    abstract SpotSize requiredSize();
}
interface Parkable { boolean park(ParkingSpot s); }   // capability (CAN-DO)

class Car extends Vehicle implements Parkable {       // both: IS-A + CAN-DO
    Car(String plate) { super(plate); }
    SpotSize requiredSize() { return SpotSize.REGULAR; }
    public boolean park(ParkingSpot s) { return s.park(this); }
}
```
*Abstract class removes duplication; the interface adds an orthogonal capability.*

